; AX3005 carries a machine-applicable fix: the missing arms, one per
; constructor in declaration order, each `((Ctor _ ...) (todo
; "Ctor"))` with one `_` per field, inserted before the match's
; closing `)` at the column of the first written arm. `todo` types as
; anything and never returns, so the arm checks against what the
; other arms answer.
;
; A SECOND fix help on the same line brings `todo` into scope. This
; file imports IO with a name list that lacks it - measured, a name
; outside the list is AX3023, and a second `(import IO ...)` beside
; a listed one is refused - so the fix extends the list in place:
; ` todo` before the list's `)`.
;
; Applied while this case was written, both edits leave AX3042 on
; `area` and on `main` above it, whose own fixes write the tag lines;
; the third round checks clean - the two codes chain.
(import IO (exit))

(data Shape
  (Circle Int)
  (Rect Int Int)
  (Dot))

(:: area (-> Shape Int))
(fn (area s)
  (match s
    ((Circle r) (* r r))))

(:: main Int)
(fn (main) (area (Circle 2)))
